Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:25:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] flow: command arguments grammar

ORFS #4771 as of d12bf2cead, rebased onto bazel-orfs's ORFS pin and the
carries before this one. A command's <COMMAND>_ARGS holds edits to the
arguments the flow passes it, scoped by stage or call
(docs/user/CommandArguments.md); flow/scripts/args_grammar.bzl is the
grammar, in the subset of Python that is Starlark.

Where the carries met it: global_route's -backing_file (0189) is part of
the flow's arguments the grammar edits, and stays on the incremental
routes; CTS_LATENCY_OFFSETS (0241) runs before the edited
clock_tree_synthesis; the carries' variables stand beside the deprecated
ones in variables.yaml.

Not upstreamed: ORFS #4771 is open. Carried for the comparison with
OpenROAD #11755's options structs; not proposed for merge.
